Based on the thorough scene report from SceneDesignerAgent and validation from all agents, here are my final milestone rules:

```json
{
  "milestones": [
    {
      "task": "find cobblestone_stairs",
      "milestone_id": "find_cobblestone_stairs",
      "description": "Uses position_near_with_facing because this is a find/locate task. The target is the center of the cobblestone stairs pyramid at spawn-relative (10, 1, 10) — the stairs span from (6,0,6) to (14,2,14) so (10,1,10) is the volumetric center. max_distance=16 is generous since the pyramid is a large 3-tier structure visible from a distance. facing_tolerance=60° ensures the player is actually looking toward the structure, not just nearby. This rule was chosen over position_inside_box because find tasks should verify the player can SEE the target, not just be near it.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "type": "position_near_with_facing",
          "params": {
            "target": [10, 1, 10],
            "max_distance": 16,
            "facing_tolerance": 60,
            "coordinate_frame": "spawn_relative"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "task": "find beacon",
      "milestone_id": "find_beacon",
      "description": "Uses position_near_with_facing because this is a find/locate task. The target is the beacon block at spawn-relative (10, 4, 10), matching the /setblock ~10 ~4 ~10 command. max_distance=10 is tighter than the stairs milestone because the beacon is a single small block at the pyramid apex — the player must approach closer to meaningfully identify it. This tighter distance also naturally enforces the task dependency: the player must walk toward the structure (past the stairs milestone threshold) to reach the beacon milestone threshold. facing_tolerance=60° ensures the player is looking up toward the beacon at the top of the pyramid.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "type": "position_near_with_facing",
          "params": {
            "target": [10, 4, 10],
            "max_distance": 10,
            "facing_tolerance": 60,
            "coordinate_frame": "spawn_relative"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

### Design Rationale Summary

| Aspect | Milestone 1 (stairs) | Milestone 2 (beacon) |
|--------|----------------------|----------------------|
| **Rule type** | position_near_with_facing | position_near_with_facing |
| **Why this type** | "Find" task → must verify player sees target | "Find" task → must verify player sees target |
| **Target coords** | (10, 1, 10) — pyramid center | (10, 4, 10) — exact beacon block |
| **max_distance** | 16 (large structure, visible far) | 10 (small block, needs closer approach) |
| **facing_tolerance** | 60° (standard) | 60° (standard) |
| **Already satisfied at spawn?** | No — spawn faces south (~yaw 0), target is NE (~45°), angular diff ~135° > 60° | No — spawn is ~14.7 blocks away > 10 |
| **Achievable?** | Yes — confirmed via sandbox in ~5 steps | Yes — confirmed via sandbox in ~15 steps |

The distance differential (16 vs 10) naturally enforces sequential completion: the player satisfies the stairs milestone first while approaching, then must continue closer to satisfy the beacon milestone.

